# clawdmeter-daemon .env.example
#
# Copy to .env in this same directory and fill in what you need. .env is
# loaded automatically on startup (script-directory .env first, then a .env
# in the current working directory) -- no extra flags required. Real
# environment variables (export, a systemd Environment= line, etc.) always
# take priority over anything set here.
#
# Every setting below can also be passed as a CLI flag instead -- .env just
# saves retyping them on every run / lets a systemd unit stay flag-free.

# Long-lived Claude Code token (`claude setup-token`). Only needed if this
# machine's OS keychain / ~/.claude/.credentials.json isn't usable (e.g. a
# headless server with no OS keychain, like pi5 in this project).
#CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# REQUIRED (one way or another) for push mode: tells the daemon which
# device to push to. Same effect as --push-to; semicolon-separate multiple
# devices (see README for the exact syntax). Equivalent alias also
# accepted: SMALLTV_PUSH_URL
#
# Can be a raw IP (192.168.0.6) or the device's mDNS hostname
# (smalltv-f661.local, from the device's own web UI/`/api/config`
# "hostname" field) -- the hostname form survives DHCP handing the device
# a new IP, the raw-IP form doesn't. Whether the hostname form actually
# resolves depends on *this machine's* mDNS/Bonjour resolver, not the
# daemon: confirmed working from a Linux host with avahi-daemon running
# (`avahi-resolve -n <name>.local` succeeds), but did NOT resolve from a
# macOS host in one test this project did (`curl http://<name>.local/`
# timed out even though macOS ships Bonjour by default) -- root cause not
# investigated. If the hostname form doesn't work for you, fall back to
# the raw IP and re-check it after any DHCP renewal.
#CLAWDMETER_PUSH_URL=192.168.0.6

# Path to a Google service-account key JSON (Google Calendar feature,
# recommended auth method -- see README's Google Calendar section). Google's
# own standard env var name, not invented for this project. Falls back to
# ~/.clawdmeter-google-service-account.json if unset.
#GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/path/to/your-service-account-key.json
